SIGN: Wipe Wipe Wipe Wipe

471
00:16:53,250 --> 00:16:54,880
SIGN: Voooooooor Vooooooor

472
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:59,460
TAMON: I'm always making you do things 
outside of household chores, 

473
00:16:59,460 --> 00:17:02,470
TAMON: so I figured I could try to cook 
something for myself but...

474
00:17:02,470 --> 00:17:04,990
UTAGE: What were you trying to make, exactly?

475
00:17:04,990 --> 00:17:06,430
TAMON: A rolled omelet...

476
00:17:06,430 --> 00:17:12,810
SIGN: Kill...

477
00:17:06,430 --> 00:17:12,810
SIGN: Kill...

478
00:17:06,430 --> 00:17:12,810
SIGN: me....

479
00:17:06,430 --> 00:17:12,810
SIGN: me....

480
00:17:06,430 --> 00:17:12,810
SIGN: Kill...

481
00:17:06,430 --> 00:17:12,810
SIGN: Kill...

482
00:17:06,430 --> 00:17:12,810
SIGN: me....

483
00:17:06,430 --> 00:17:12,810
SIGN: me....

484
00:17:06,710 --> 00:17:12,810
EGG: Kill... me... Kill... me... 
Kill... me... Kill... me...

485
00:17:06,710 --> 00:17:09,690
TAMON: Forget doing justice to a life
brought into this world, 

486
00:17:09,690 --> 00:17:12,810
TAMON: I ended up ruthlessly murdering it 
and abandoning it.

487
00:17:12,810 --> 00:17:15,450
UTAGE: Now, now, everyone struggles at first.

488
00:17:15,450 --> 00:17:18,650
TAMON: I'm going on a voluntary hiatus from work 
until I can properly fry an egg.

489
00:17:18,650 --> 00:17:19,930
UTAGE: Wait a minute!

490
00:17:19,930 --> 00:17:21,339
UTAGE: Even if you can't fry an egg, 

491
00:17:21,339 --> 00:17:24,200
UTAGE: there is something you're very good 
at making, Tamon-kun!

492
00:17:24,869 --> 00:17:26,579
UTAGE: Making your fans smile!

493
00:17:27,619 --> 00:17:35,630
GIRLS: I love you! I love you!

494
00:17:28,980 --> 00:17:31,420
UTAGE: You're able to make all those smiles!

495
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:35,630
SIGN: Church of Tamon

496
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:34,370
UTAGE: If that doesn't make you a top chef, 
I don't know what does!

497
00:17:34,370 --> 00:17:35,630
UTAGE: Have more confidence in yourself!

498
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:40,220
TAMON: I'm not sure if I fully understand, 
 but I somehow feel like I can keep going.

499
00:17:42,700 --> 00:17:44,580
UTAGE: That's Fujita-san, his manager.

500
00:17:44,580 --> 00:17:46,470
FUJITA: That was impressive.

501
00:17:46,470 --> 00:17:50,560
FUJITA: You somehow immediately got Tamon 
out of his nervous breakdown mode.

502
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:55,150
FUJITA: I'm shocked.

503
00:17:56,000 --> 00:18:00,450
FUJITA: I never thought he'd be rehabilitated 
this much just by hiring a housekeeper.

504
00:18:00,450 --> 00:18:03,290
FUJITA: He's actually been 
obediently working lately.

505
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:06,070
UTAGE: Well, household chores get 
so tiresome when you're busy.

506
00:18:06,070 --> 00:18:11,280
TAMON: Fujita-san, you just see me as a cash cow, 
but Kinoshita-san doesn't.

507
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:12,940
TAMON: I don't think. Probably.

508
00:18:13,430 --> 00:18:16,690
UTAGE: He looks like an abandoned puppy 
that doesn't trust humans anymore.

509
00:18:16,690 --> 00:18:19,840
FUJITA: By the way, just how much 
counts as household chores?

510
00:18:20,730 --> 00:18:24,120
UTAGE: Honestly, pretty much anything, 
depending on the customer.

511
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:26,090
UTAGE: I even go shopping 
or take pets out for a walk.

512
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:28,960
FUJITA: I see.

513
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:31,490
FUJITA: So practicing for the meet-and-greet 
and going shopping together

514
00:18:31,490 --> 00:18:33,310
FUJITA: counts as "household chores."

515
00:18:34,310 --> 00:18:36,010
UTAGE: I'm so sorry!

516
00:18:36,010 --> 00:18:38,520
UTAGE: One wrong move, and I could've 
caused a huge misunderstanding!

517
00:18:38,520 --> 00:18:40,480
TAMON: Kinoshita-san didn't do anything wrong!

518
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:42,940
TAMON: If you're going to kill someone, kill me!

519
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:56,040
FUJITA: Please continue helping with all of 
Tamon's "household chores" from now on!

520
00:18:57,110 --> 00:18:57,860
UTAGE: Huh?

521
00:18:58,250 --> 00:19:02,870
FUJITA: This is embarrassing to admit, but we're 
a small little agency with no connections.

522
00:19:02,870 --> 00:19:05,180
FUJITA: We absolutely don't have enough people.

523
00:19:05,180 --> 00:19:07,680
FUJITA: Honestly, you're a lifesaver!

524
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:12,600
FUJITA: Now, then... I have to go buy some 
maritozzi for a certain selfish gorilla, 

525
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:14,640
FUJITA: so take care of the 
nervous breakdown zombie for me!

526
00:19:16,780 --> 00:19:17,850
UTAGE: Um...

527
00:19:17,850 --> 00:19:20,930
UTAGE: So basically... anything goes.

528
00:19:22,050 --> 00:19:24,110
TAMON: I want you to accept all of me.

529
00:19:24,570 --> 00:19:26,820
UTAGE: Personal desires... begone!

530
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:28,950
TAMON: Are you all right, Kinoshita-san?

531
00:19:28,950 --> 00:19:30,700
UTAGE: Yes, I'm fine.

532
00:19:31,060 --> 00:19:32,570
UTAGE: Calm yourself, Utage.

533
00:19:32,570 --> 00:19:35,430
UTAGE: You're just helping Tamon-kun out 
with his idol work.

534
00:19:35,430 --> 00:19:37,210
TAMON: Please don't push yourself too hard.

535
00:19:37,870 --> 00:19:42,780
UTAGE: When Tamon-kun was sixteen, 
he came to Tokyo all alone for his audition.

536
00:19:44,380 --> 00:19:46,510
UTAGE: From everything I've personally seen, 

537
00:19:46,510 --> 00:19:50,260
UTAGE: it seems like his manager's not 
taking care of him that much.

538
00:19:50,610 --> 00:19:53,400
UTAGE: He doesn't get along that well 
with the other members either.

539
00:19:54,290 --> 00:20:00,020
UTAGE: Of course he'd rely on a busybody fangirl
 that just happened to come into his life.

540
00:20:00,390 --> 00:20:05,190
UTAGE: Yes. I'm just a convenient fan to Tamon-kun.

541
00:20:05,520 --> 00:20:09,160
UTAGE: Then I'm just going to have to work 
my hardest so I don't let him down...

542
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:10,990
UTAGE: As the person in charge of household chores.

543
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:14,400
UTAGE: Oh, I wonder if it's from work...

544
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:17,330
UTAGE: A candid shot!

545
00:20:19,290 --> 00:20:21,450
UTAGE: Oh, I'm sorry to yell like that 
while you're working.

546
00:20:21,450 --> 00:20:22,710
TAMON: It's fine.

547
00:20:22,710 --> 00:20:25,710
TAMON: I was just thinking that you're 
so interesting, Kinoshita-san.

548
00:20:25,710 --> 00:20:28,930
UTAGE: Huh? Am I?

549
00:20:28,930 --> 00:20:30,050
TAMON: Yes.

550
00:20:30,050 --> 00:20:32,270
TAMON: You just suddenly yell sometimes.

551
00:20:32,270 --> 00:20:34,150
UTAGE: All of your fans are like this.

552
00:20:34,470 --> 00:20:37,060
TAMON: I don't know about anybody else. But...

553
00:20:37,060 --> 00:20:39,690
TAMON: If anything, to me right now...

554
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:43,360
TAMON: You're special, Kinoshita-san.

555
00:20:45,740 --> 00:20:47,240
UTAGE: Oh, come on!

556
00:20:47,240 --> 00:20:49,030
UTAGE: Jeez, Tamon-kun.

557
00:20:51,650 --> 00:20:53,990
UTAGE: He's just excellent at fanservice, 

558
00:20:53,990 --> 00:20:56,490
UTAGE: and he just happened to have 
a fan right in front of him.

559
00:20:57,040 --> 00:20:59,960
UTAGE: That's why he instantly says 
stuff that makes me happy.

560
00:21:02,350 --> 00:21:04,670
UTAGE: At first, I was just trying to escape reality.

561
00:21:07,380 --> 00:21:09,260
FRIEND: You're so boring, Uta-chan.

562
00:21:09,260 --> 00:21:10,170
UTAGE: Huh?

563
00:21:10,170 --> 00:21:12,630
FRIEND: I'm the only one who ever 
talks in our conversations.

564
00:21:12,630 --> 00:21:15,890
FRIEND: It's good to accommodate others, 
but that's all you ever do.

565
00:21:15,890 --> 00:21:18,560
FRIEND: I have no idea what you're even thinking.

566
00:21:20,770 --> 00:21:26,070
UTAGE: When I'd been flattened like an empty husk, 
you just happened to cross my eye.

567
00:21:26,070 --> 00:21:28,690
16 YEAR OLD TAMON: I want to make everyone in the world smile.

568
00:21:28,690 --> 00:21:32,660
UTAGE: And you happened to say something I'd never 
say even if I'd been reborn a hundred times.

569
00:21:37,470 --> 00:21:39,200
UTAGE: An encounter with the unknown.

570
00:21:39,670 --> 00:21:44,290
UTAGE: Ever since I learned of your existence, 
every day's been so fun and going by so fast!

571
00:21:45,750 --> 00:21:49,210
UTAGE: Your dream became my dream.

572
00:21:49,210 --> 00:21:52,430
UTAGE: That's why I don't need to be special.

573
00:21:52,430 --> 00:21:53,870
UTAGE: He looked at me!

574
00:21:53,870 --> 00:21:57,060
UTAGE: You're special to me, so just 
having you show me your dream...

575
00:21:57,060 --> 00:21:59,430
UTAGE: Huh? That necklace...

576
00:21:59,430 --> 00:22:01,770
UTAGE: ...makes me so happy.

577
00:22:02,550 --> 00:22:04,590
UTAGE: Or so I thought...

578
00:22:05,610 --> 00:22:06,710
UTAGE: Huh?

579
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:10,220
TAMON: You're special, Kinoshita-san.

580
00:22:11,660 --> 00:22:14,180
UTAGE: What was that just now?

581
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:30,250
LYRICS: Uh huh...

582
00:22:30,250 --> 00:22:32,290
LYRICS: Na na na...

583
00:22:32,290 --> 00:22:35,340
LYRICS: Uh huh...

584
00:22:37,470 --> 00:22:46,890
LYRICS: I wonder what the world 
would look like without you

585
00:22:47,730 --> 00:22:52,610
LYRICS: When I look back, 
you've always been by my side

586
00:22:52,610 --> 00:22:57,530
LYRICS: Teaching me what "warmth" 
and "happiness" feel like

587
00:22:57,530 --> 00:23:00,320
LYRICS: A speedboat sails across the endless skies

588
00:23:00,320 --> 00:23:02,870
LYRICS: An unwavering course, 
a straight shot down the middle

589
00:23:02,870 --> 00:23:05,490
LYRICS: An unbreakable red balloon 
found nowhere else

590
00:23:05,490 --> 00:23:08,750
LYRICS: Is this "fate"? Or just a "coincidence"?

591
00:23:09,040 --> 00:23:13,840
LYRICS: Like a wilted flower coming back to life

592
00:23:13,840 --> 00:23:16,380
LYRICS: A light that shines

593
00:23:16,380 --> 00:23:19,380
LYRICS: Through the impossibly dark night

594
00:23:19,380 --> 00:23:20,680
LYRICS: (Light of your soul)

595
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:22,050
LYRICS: I wanted to grasp it

596
00:23:22,050 --> 00:23:23,340
LYRICS: (I love you so)

597
00:23:23,340 --> 00:23:24,390
LYRICS: So I strived for it

598
00:23:24,390 --> 00:23:27,100
LYRICS: Wanna keep going, wanna keep growing

599
00:23:27,100 --> 00:23:30,790
LYRICS: Bringing our flowers and dreams 
into full bloom
